  "timeYesterdayAt": "{hour, select, one{yesterday {time}} other{yesterday {time}}}",
  "@timeYesterdayAt": {
    "description": "A moment yesterday: the word for yesterday and a clock time like 23:23 or 11:23 PM. Lower case: it can follow other words. {hour} is \"one\" when the clock time's hour is 1 (1:05, 01:05, 1:05 PM), else \"other\", for languages with an article before the time (Spanish \"a la 1:05\" but \"a las 23:05\", Portuguese \"à 1:05\" but \"às 23:05\", Italian \"all’1:05\"). English says the same in both cases.",
